%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%BoundingBox: 0 0 612 612
%%Title: Moss Goes to the Sea, page 11: the sea sings
/Seed where { pop } { /Seed 12 def } ifelse  Seed srand
(lib/cb_book.ps) run
cb-ground
270 cb-night [0.32 0.34 0.58] cb-sky-wash
300 455 10 113 cb-stars
440 380 40 cb-moon-paint
270 cb-sea cb-sea-paint
% the moon's path on the water
0 1 14 { /i exch def
  newpath 440 i 10 mul 10 add sub 260 i 15 mul sub moveto 30 i 4 mul add 0 rlineto
  cb-moon cb-rgb << /Width 3 /Taper 0.7 /Waver 0.4 >> pkliner } for
-9 600 230 30 [0.75 0.85 0.95] 1.1 cb-waves
-20 600 180 40 [0.75 0.85 0.95] 1.3 cb-waves
newpath -9 -9 moveto -9 100 lineto 200 110 400 70 621 60 curveto 621 -9 lineto closepath cb-sand 0.85 cb-wash
newpath -9 100 moveto 200 110 400 70 621 60 curveto [0.95 0.97 1] cb-rgb << /Width 3 /Taper 0.2 >> pkliner
/cb-face 1 def
170 86 18 cb-moss
cb-paper cb-rgb
(There was the sea, big and silver under the moon. And it sang:) 60 584 492 /center cb-text pop
cb-fontit findfont 30 scalefont setfont (hush . . . hush . . . hush.) 306 486 showctr
11 cb-folio
showpage
